Working Title: DEBUF: Destroying Evil Baddie Universally Forever
Concept Statement: Using incremental style benefits from a elder god, RPG your way through a set amount of randomly assorted bosses and areas until you can defeat the BBEG, utilising debuffs, specific vulnerabilities and out of dungeon effects to get the upperhand.
Genres: RPG, Rougelite, Incremental
Target Audience: RPG Intermediates/Veterans 30-45 Softly Leaning Male ESRB Mature (17+)
Unique Selling Points: Debuffing led design with a strong meta progression elements, and a loadout structure. Eldritch horror where you are alongside the horror not wholy or mostly pit against it.

Player Experience and Game POV: The player is the first adventurer to non violently and not offend the elder god "pixie" character in 10000 years. A genteel homely homebase area with a gothic torture dungeon aesthetic as you travel the backside of the BBEG's castle. The fantasy is that your character, by being immortal through the character that helps you, allows you to gain power through modifiers for the run, to build up a pallete of abilities that you would like to inflict unto enemies, and the BBEG in the end. The emotions of the player going through the struggle of managing building up the inital load out is one of frustration, yet pay off, as they manage to defeat certain bosses and elites.
